        <h2>OON</h2>
        <p><strong>OON</strong> is a co-creation by Sarah Palu and Johanna Tarkkanen. They met in 2016 and sat down together to listen to the silence. From that silence music started to unfold like water from a spring. This music is the essence of OON.</p>
        <p><em>“There was a long pause where the silence became almost visceral, a calling in the air. The music from the kantele started and a journey began. The music felt circular and though I was still, it felt I was being unravelled, threads unknotting and knotting, an embroidery of skin. The music stopped gradually after a while but the memory hung in the air. It is still in the air, though I am now thousands of miles away. This is sublime and delicate work, an experience that will stay with me. We need to delve into crevices and cracks like this: tastes that linger; experiences that touch us; the scent of time.”</em><br /><strong>Caroline Smith</strong>, Programme Leader Creative Learning, Barbican Guildhall</p>
        <p>OON was selected to represent Finland at the UNM festival 2019 for Nordic composers and sound artists in Piteå Sweden with their piece “Metsänkellot” (Forest Chimes).</p>
        <p>#OONsounds #kantelemeditation<br /><a href="https://www.instagram.com/oonsounds/" rel="noopener">www.instagram.com/oonsounds/</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>

